#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 3496..4388
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/3
msgid ""
"...No thanks. It... doesn't suit me.\n"
msgstr ""
"……不了。那……不适合我。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 4444..4862
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/4
msgid ""
"Too bad for you.\n"
msgstr ""
"算你倒霉。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 4945..6032
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/5
msgid ""
"You know, the \"V\" in the peace sign comes from\n"
"the \"V\" in \"Victory.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"和平手势的\"V\"来自\n"
"\"Victory\"（胜利）的\"V\"。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 6199..6882
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/6
msgid ""
"When did it start standing for peace?\n"
msgstr ""
"它何时开始代表和平？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 6952..7648
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/7
msgid ""
"I am not completely sure... but\n"
msgstr ""
"我也不太确定……不过\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 7774..8832
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/8
msgid ""
"I guess it came out of the protest movement\n"
"against the Vietnam War.\n"
msgstr ""
"我想是出自反越南战争的\n"
"抗议运动吧。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 8888..9724
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/9
msgid ""
"Oh, and don't turn your hand around when you do\n"
"it,\n"
msgstr ""
"哦，还有，做的时候别把手转过来\n"
"，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0040_000_0
#. timeline 9766..10699
#: codec/1/185/0xb9250/10
msgid ""
"especially around British people. It is insulting.\n"
msgstr ""
"尤其在英国人面前。那是侮辱。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 487..1072
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/0
msgid ""
"So you live alone now?\n"
msgstr ""
"所以你现在一个人住？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 1086..2605
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/1
msgid ""
"No, not alone. I've been living in school dormitories\n"
"since I started junior high.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，不是一个人。我上初中起\n"
"就一直住学校宿舍。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 2688..4304
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/2
msgid ""
"After my mother died, my relatives took me in,\n"
"but... they were not my real family.\n"
msgstr ""
"母亲去世后，亲戚收留了我，\n"
"但……他们不是我的家人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 4332..4709
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/3
msgid ""
"You didn't fit in there?\n"
msgstr ""
"你融不进去？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 4722..5544
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/4
msgid ""
"In a way... My aunts were kind to me and all...\n"
msgstr ""
"某种程度……姨妈们对我也好……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 5698..7077
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/5
msgid ""
"But I know how difficult it must have been to\n"
"suddenly have a child thrust into their lives.\n"
msgstr ""
"但我知道，突然有个孩子闯进\n"
"她们的生活有多难。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 7133..7927
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/6
msgid ""
"When you live with someone, there are no secrets.\n"
msgstr ""
"和人一起生活，是藏不住秘密的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 8108..8832
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/7
msgid ""
"I could tell my being there was a burden on them...\n"
msgstr ""
"我看得出我的存在是他们的负担……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 9209..9724
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/8
msgid ""
"Sounds like a rough childhood.\n"
msgstr ""
"你童年听着挺苦。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 9766..10922
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/9
msgid ""
"I would not say that. I was lucky just to have\n"
"people to take me in.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不这么觉得。有人肯收留我\n"
"已经很幸运了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 10964..12162
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/10
msgid ""
"There are huérfanos living out in the streets\n"
"because their mothers died.\n"
msgstr ""
"还有孤儿因为母亲死了\n"
"流落街头。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 12246..13165
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/11
msgid ""
"It is even worse in countries with frequent civil\n"
"wars.\n"
msgstr ""
"在战乱频发的国家\n"
"更惨。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 13221..14113
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/12
msgid ""
"So who am I to complain about my childhood?\n"
msgstr ""
"我哪有资格抱怨自己的童年？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 14154..14628
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/13
msgid ""
"You're a pretty tough kid, you know?\n"
msgstr ""
"你这孩子挺坚强的嘛。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 14656..15562
#: codec/1/185/0xb95f0/14
msgid ""
"...Not at all. I am not strong at all.\n"
msgstr ""
"……才没。我一点不坚强。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 473..1003
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/0
msgid ""
"I have a favor to ask you, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE，我想求你件事。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 1044..1226
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/1
msgid ""
"Name it.\n"
msgstr ""
"说。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 1267..2215
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/2
msgid ""
"I want to you to give me a job here. I want to help\n"
"out.\n"
msgstr ""
"我想让你在这给我个工作。我想帮\n"
"忙。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 2243..3148
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/3
msgid ""
"You sure? You just went through a hell of a time.\n"
msgstr ""
"你确定？你刚经历了一场大难。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 3287..3970
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/4
msgid ""
"You should probably take it easy until you're\n"
"settled.\n"
msgstr ""
"你最好先放松，等安顿下来\n"
"再说。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 4012..4904
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/5
msgid ""
"Thank you. But there must be something I can do.\n"
msgstr ""
"谢谢。但我总得做点什么。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 4945..6116
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/6
msgid ""
"You would not want me near a gun, but I am a\n"
"decent cook.\n"
msgstr ""
"你别让我碰枪，不过我做菜还\n"
"不错。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 6171..6826
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/7
msgid ""
"Now there's a skill we can use.\n"
msgstr ""
"这本事正好用得上。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 6854..7885
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/8
msgid ""
"Put me on the mess hall team - I think I can handle\n"
"it.\n"
msgstr ""
"把我排到食堂组，我觉得我能\n"
"应付。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 8010..9250
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/9
msgid ""
"Once I get used to it, I'll even add in some Costa\n"
"Rican recipes.\n"
msgstr ""
"等我习惯了，我还会加一些哥斯达黎加\n"
"菜谱。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_paz0180_000_0
#. timeline 9292..9780
#: codec/1/185/0xb9b50/10
msgid ""
"Sounds like a plan.\n"
msgstr ""
"就这么定了。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba290/0
msgid ""
"Bosque del Alba means \"forest of dawn.\" Naturally,\n"
"it is situated on the east coast.\n"
msgstr ""
"Bosque del Alba 的意思是“黎明之林”。自然，\n"
"它位于东海岸。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba290/1
msgid ""
"It is your standard tropical rainforest, everything\n"
"you'd imagine in a jungle.\n"
msgstr ""
"就是标准的热带雨林，你能想象到的\n"
"丛林里的一切。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba290/2
msgid ""
"No sign of morning sun here.\n"
msgstr ""
"这里见不到晨光。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba290/3
msgid ""
"The foliage is too thick for direct sunlight to hit\n"
"the floor.\n"
msgstr ""
"枝叶太茂密，阳光无法直接照到\n"
"地面。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba290/4
msgid ""
"I do not know how easy it will be making your way\n"
"through here.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不知道你在这里穿行会有多\n"
"容易。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba290/5
msgid ""
"I'll be fine. This isn't my first trip to a jungle.\n"
msgstr ""
"我没事。这又不是我第一次进丛林。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 473..1727
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/0
msgid ""
"The mercenaries' supply base is situated on\n"
"elevated ground by the coast.\n"
msgstr ""
"雇佣兵的补给基地坐落在海岸边的\n"
"高地上。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 1825..2981
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/1
msgid ""
"I heard them call it \"Puerto del Alba\" - \"Port of\n"
"Dawn.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"我听到他们叫它“Puerto del Alba”——“黎明\n"
"港”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 3051..3845
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/2
msgid ""
"They have perfect visibility of the area from up\n"
"there.\n"
msgstr ""
"从上面，他们能看清\n"
"这一带。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 3928..4709
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/3
msgid ""
"We did our best to sneak in undetected, but...\n"
msgstr ""
"我们尽力潜入不被发现，可……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 4959..5544
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/4
msgid ""
"one of the guards spotted us, and we...\n"
msgstr ""
"一个守卫发现了我们，我们……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 5572..5823
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/5
msgid ""
"What is it?\n"
msgstr ""
"怎么？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 5837..6840
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/6
msgid ""
"...I'm sorry, you'll have to ask Professor Gálvez the\n"
"rest.\n"
msgstr ""
"……抱歉，剩下的你得去问 Gálvez\n"
"教授。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 6868..7718
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/7
msgid ""
"...It's OK. You've been through a lot.\n"
msgstr ""
"……没事。你受苦了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 7732..8735
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/8
msgid ""
"I am sorry, I... I just cannot...\n"
msgstr ""
"对不起，我……我说不下去……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0030_000_0
#. timeline 8749..10031
#: codec/1/186/0xba530/9
msgid ""
"You did great, Paz. I won't let your efforts go\n"
"wasted.\n"
msgstr ""
"你做得很好，Paz。我不会让你\n"
"白费。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba8b0/0
msgid ""
"This is a tropical rainforest, just like Bosque del\n"
"Alba.\n"
msgstr ""
"这是热带雨林，就像阿尔巴森林\n"
"一样。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba8b0/1
msgid ""
"The temperature and humidity can be brutal. El\n"
"Cenegal means \"Place of Mud.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"温湿度可能很严酷。埃尔\n"
"塞内加尔意为“泥泞之地”。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba8b0/2
msgid ""
"Mud. Great. I'll watch my step.\n"
msgstr ""
"泥巴。好极了。我会小心的。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba8b0/3
msgid ""
"This area often gets flooded by the river.\n"
msgstr ""
"这一带常被河水淹没。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba8b0/4
msgid ""
"There are canals here and there carved out by the\n"
"water.\n"
msgstr ""
"这里有水流冲刷出来的\n"
"一条条水道。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba8b0/5
msgid ""
"Good places to hide.\n"
msgstr ""
"藏身好地方。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xba8b0/6
msgid ""
"But they'll also make it harder for you to see. Be\n"
"careful, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"但它们也会让你更难看清周围。小\n"
"心，斯内克。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 445..1212
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/0
msgid ""
"There should be a suspension bridge around there.\n"
msgstr ""
"那附近应该有座吊桥。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 1239..1713
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/1
msgid ""
"In lowlands like this?\n"
msgstr ""
"这种低地会有？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 1769..2633
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/2
msgid ""
"The ground nearby is harder and higher than usual.\n"
msgstr ""
"附近地面比一般更硬更高。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 2716..3594
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/3
msgid ""
"The river cut through it, eventually creating a\n"
"valley.\n"
msgstr ""
"河流穿凿而过，最终形成了一道\n"
"山谷。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 3636..4597
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/4
msgid ""
"There might be another way to get across the\n"
"river somewhere.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许还有别的办法可以渡过\n"
"这条河。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 4597..5349
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/5
msgid ""
"I wouldn't want to run into someone on the bridge.\n"
msgstr ""
"我可不想在桥上撞见人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 5391..6687
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/6
msgid ""
"The valley tends to be misty, so you might not be\n"
"able to see the water from up there.\n"
msgstr ""
"山谷里常常雾气弥漫，所以你在上面可能看\n"
"不到水面。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0050_000_0
#. timeline 6770..7314
#: codec/1/186/0xbab50/7
msgid ""
"Fall and it'll leave more than a bump.\n"
msgstr ""
"掉下去可不只是摔个包。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xbae80/0
msgid ""
"When a river floods an area, the banks can\n"
"collapse, creating a marsh.\n"
msgstr ""
"河流淹没一片区域时，河岸可能\n"
"坍塌，形成沼泽。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xbae80/1
msgid ""
"You see a lot of them around here.\n"
msgstr ""
"这附近很多。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xbae80/2
msgid ""
"I'll need to watch the noise my feet make in el\n"
"cenegal.\n"
msgstr ""
"我得留意自己在埃尔\n"
"塞内加尔里脚下发出的声响。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xbae80/3
msgid ""
"There's a marsh on the other side of the river, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"河对岸也有片沼泽。\n"

#: codec/1/186/0xbae80/4
msgid ""
"The suspension bridge will take you there.\n"
msgstr ""
"吊桥能通到那边。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 445..1630
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/0
msgid ""
"The river running through here is Río del Jade, or\n"
"\"the Jade River.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"流经这里的是里奥德尔哈德河，即\n"
"“翡翠河”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 1657..2438
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/1
msgid ""
"Jade? Are there minerals around here?\n"
msgstr ""
"翡翠？这附近有矿？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 2452..3287
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/2
msgid ""
"No, it refers to the color of the water.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，是指水色。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 3357..4040
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/3
msgid ""
"You'll have to go to Guatemala for jade.\n"
msgstr ""
"翡翠得去危地马拉才有。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 4096..5475
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/4
msgid ""
"Hmm... Doesn't look all that pretty from where I'm\n"
"standing.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯……从我站的地方看，可没那么\n"
"漂亮。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 5517..6673
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/5
msgid ""
"We're still in the rainy season, so the river's a little\n"
"muddy.\n"
msgstr ""
"现在还是雨季，所以河水有点\n"
"浑浊。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 6715..7606
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/6
msgid ""
"It'll return to normal once the dry season starts.\n"
msgstr ""
"旱季一到就会恢复。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 7648..8554
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/7
msgid ""
"Rivers are an important means of transport around\n"
"here.\n"
msgstr ""
"这一带的河流是重要的\n"
"运输手段。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 8609..9822
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/8
msgid ""
"They're relatively calm, and there are plenty of\n"
"canals along the coast, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们相对平静，而且沿岸还有\n"
"很多运河。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 9863..10978
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/9
msgid ""
"A boat'd be more than enough to transport some\n"
"good-sized cargo.\n"
msgstr ""
"用一艘船来运输一些\n"
"大件货物绰绰有余。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 10978..11619
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/10
msgid ""
"Like... a nuclear weapon?\n"
msgstr ""
"比如……核武器？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 11967..12887
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/11
msgid ""
"We don't know enough yet. I'll keep looking.\n"
msgstr ""
"目前情报还不够。我继续查。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0070_000_0
#. timeline 12914..13221
#: codec/1/187/0xbb080/12
#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/29
msgid ""
"Thank you, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"谢谢你，SNAKE。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 445..1727
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/0
msgid ""
"There's a lot of banana cultivation along Costa\n"
"Rica's Caribbean coast.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加的加勒比海岸沿线\n"
"种植着大量香蕉。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 1839..2702
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/1
msgid ""
"The area's dotted with banana plantations.\n"
msgstr ""
"这一带遍布香蕉种植园。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 2772..3524
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/2
msgid ""
"Bananas have been Costa Rica's main crop\n"
msgstr ""
"香蕉是哥斯达黎加主要作物，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 3538..4611
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/3
msgid ""
"since they were introduced from Panama in the\n"
"19th century.\n"
msgstr ""
"自从19世纪它们从巴拿马\n"
"传入以来。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 4695..5447
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/4
msgid ""
"They bring in a fair amount of foreign currency.\n"
msgstr ""
"带来了相当可观的外汇收入。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 5503..6227
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/5
msgid ""
"A real fruta de oro, huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"真是黄金果实啊。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 6241..7453
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/6
msgid ""
"Si. But exporting all those bananas requires a ton\n"
"of land.\n"
msgstr ""
"是的。但出口所有这些香蕉需要\n"
"大片土地。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 7537..8219
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/7
msgid ""
"Hence all the plantations.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以才有了这么多种植园。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 8261..9543
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/8
msgid ""
"Clearing all that forest just to grow bananas robs\n"
"animals of their habitats.\n"
msgstr ""
"为了种香蕉而砍伐所有那些森林，剥夺了\n"
"动物的栖息地。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0080_000_0
#. timeline 9654..10546
#: codec/1/187/0xbb510/9
msgid ""
"I do not know how good that is for Costa Rica in\n"
"the end.\n"
msgstr ""
"不知这最终对哥斯达黎加\n"
"有多大好处。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 459..1267
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/0
msgid ""
"Panama disease was rampant here about 20 years\n"
"ago,\n"
msgstr ""
"约20年前，巴拿马病在这里\n"
"肆虐，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 1393..2284
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/1
msgid ""
"putting a lot of banana plantations out of business.\n"
msgstr ""
"让许多香蕉种植园倒闭。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 2354..2716
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/2
msgid ""
"Panama disease?\n"
msgstr ""
"巴拿马病？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 2786..3413
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/3
msgid ""
"It is caused by a type of fungus.\n"
msgstr ""
"由一种真菌引起。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 3524..4695
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/4
msgid ""
"Apparently it killed off almost all the banana\n"
"species that used to grow here.\n"
msgstr ""
"据说它几乎杀死了这里曾经生长的\n"
"所有香蕉品种。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 4736..5154
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/5
msgid ""
"How could that happen?\n"
msgstr ""
"怎么会这样？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 5224..5893
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/6
msgid ""
"Cultivated bananas do not produce seeds.\n"
msgstr ""
"栽培香蕉不结种子。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 5948..7481
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/7
msgid ""
"You have to remove and transplant part of the\n"
"stem yourself. You plant them in the fields.\n"
msgstr ""
"你得亲手切下茎的一部分来移植，\n"
"再种到田里。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 7523..8233
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/8
msgid ""
"So you've got acres of identical plants?\n"
msgstr ""
"所以你有大片相同作物？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 8275..9487
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/9
msgid ""
"Si. When one plant is infected, the disease spreads\n"
"quickly.\n"
msgstr ""
"对。一株染病，\n"
"就会迅速蔓延。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 9599..10407
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/10
msgid ""
"Species lacking genetic diversity become weak.\n"
msgstr ""
"缺基因多样性的物种会变弱。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 10504..11075
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/11
msgid ""
"They grow different bananas today,\n"
msgstr ""
"如今他们种另一种香蕉，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0090_000_0
#. timeline 11103..11981
#: codec/1/187/0xbb8b0/12
msgid ""
"ones said to be resistant to Panama disease.\n"
msgstr ""
"据说能抵抗巴拿马病。\n"

#: codec/1/187/0xbbd10/0
msgid ""
"Costa Rica has several active volcanoes, Irazú\n"
"being one of them.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加有几座活火山，\n"
"伊拉苏是其中之一。\n"

#: codec/1/187/0xbbd10/1
msgid ""
"That's where \"Camino de Lava\" comes from, huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"所以才有\"熔岩之路\"这名字？\n"

#: codec/1/187/0xbbd10/2
msgid ""
"The tropical dry forests around here are quite\n"
"different from our rainforests.\n"
msgstr ""
"这一带的热带干林\n"
"和我们的雨林大不相同。\n"

#: codec/1/187/0xbbd10/3
msgid ""
"They lose their leaves in the dry season.\n"
msgstr ""
"旱季时它们会落叶。\n"

#: codec/1/187/0xbbd10/4
msgid ""
"Tropical forests are not all thick jungles. A few of\n"
"them even have cacti.\n"
msgstr ""
"热带森林并非都是密林，\n"
"有些甚至长着仙人掌。\n"

#: codec/1/187/0xbbd10/5
msgid ""
"Some of Costa Rica's greatest assets are its\n"
"diverse forests and natural landscapes.\n"
msgstr ""
"哥斯达黎加最宝贵的财富之一，\n"
"就是多样的森林与自然景观。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 445..1588
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/0
msgid ""
"Aldea de los Despiertos means \"Village of the\n"
"Awake.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"Aldea de los Despiertos意为\n"
"\"清醒者之村\"。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 1936..2229
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/1
msgid ""
"Weird name.\n"
msgstr ""
"这名字真怪。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 2270..3510
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/2
msgid ""
"The area's littered with coffee fields and there's a\n"
"factory nearby.\n"
msgstr ""
"这一带遍地咖啡田，\n"
"附近还有座工厂。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 3608..4569
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/3
msgid ""
"The villagers are fans of coffee, so...\n"
msgstr ""
"村民都是咖啡迷，所以……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 4806..6185
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/4
msgid ""
"They don't get much sleep, huh? They've got a\n"
"sense of humor all right.\n"
msgstr ""
"难怪他们睡不好，\n"
"还挺有幽默感。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 6283..7397
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/5
msgid ""
"I cannot believe they would take over a place like\n"
"this and use it as a prison.\n"
msgstr ""
"真不敢相信他们竟占领这种地方\n"
"当监狱用。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 7481..8763
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/6
msgid ""
"It is unforgiveable. For both la CIA and the thugs\n"
"they employ.\n"
msgstr ""
"不可原谅。CIA和他们雇的\n"
"暴徒都一样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 8832..9557
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/7
msgid ""
"All the villagers wanted was to live in peace.\n"
msgstr ""
"村民们只想平静地生活。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 9654..10490
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/8
msgid ""
"What gives la CIA the right to crush them like\n"
"that?!\n"
msgstr ""
"CIA凭什么这样\n"
"践踏他们？！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 10560..11438
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/9
msgid ""
"They don't care about anyone's rights but their\n"
"own.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们只顾自己权利，\n"
"不管别人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 11674..12204
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/10
msgid ""
"It's just the way some people are.\n"
msgstr ""
"有些人就是这样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 12260..12705
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/11
msgid ""
"You really think so?\n"
msgstr ""
"你真这么想？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0120_000_0
#. timeline 12747..14015
#: codec/1/188/0xbc2a0/12
msgid ""
"Don't worry. It just gives me the right to teach\n"
"them a lesson.\n"
msgstr ""
"别担心。这正好让我有理由\n"
"教训他们一顿。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 445..2159
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/0
msgid ""
"La CIA has taken control of this coffee factory,\n"
"too. All to produce its drugs...\n"
msgstr ""
"CIA也控制了这家咖啡厂。\n"
"全是为了制毒……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 2215..3204
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/1
msgid ""
"It was famous once, for its fine beans.\n"
msgstr ""
"它曾以优质咖啡豆闻名。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 3482..4722
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/2
msgid ""
"Cafetal Aroma Encantado... \"Enchanting Aroma,\"\n"
"huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"Cafetal Aroma Encantado……“迷人香气”，\n"
"是吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 4764..5823
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/3
msgid ""
"Si. Once we've thrown the mercenaries out of\n"
"Costa Rica,\n"
msgstr ""
"Si。等我们把雇佣兵赶出\n"
"哥斯达黎加，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 5935..6701
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/4
msgid ""
"I know it will make wonderful coffee again.\n"
msgstr ""
"我相信它能再产出好咖啡。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 6743..7370
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/5
msgid ""
"And then you must come and try some, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"到时候你一定要来尝尝，SNAKE。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 7370..9306
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/6
msgid ""
"Sounds great. I wouldn't mind a cuppa joe after all\n"
"this is over. Oh, wait...\n"
msgstr ""
"听着不错。等这一切结束，我倒不介意\n"
"来杯咖啡。哦，等等……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 9334..9557
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/7
msgid ""
"What is wrong?\n"
msgstr ""
"怎么了？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 9599..11215
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/8
msgid ""
"No, I... just remembered this guy I knew who wasn't\n"
"big on coffee. English.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，我……刚想起一个认识的人，他不太\n"
"爱喝咖啡。英国人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 11354..12552
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/9
msgid ""
"\"Get rid of that muddy water and get a cup of\n"
"black tea down your gob,\" he'd say.\n"
msgstr ""
"“别喝那泥水了，来杯红茶\n"
"灌进你嘴里，”他总这么说。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0130_000_0
#. timeline 12552..13918
#: codec/1/188/0xbc730/10
msgid ""
"Ha! That's too bad for him - it is delicious.\n"
msgstr ""
"哈！他亏了，这咖啡好喝。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 445..1727
#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/0
msgid ""
"As I said before, building railroads in Costa Rica\n"
"was a dangerous job.\n"
msgstr ""
"我说过，在哥斯达黎加修铁路\n"
"是危险的工作。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 1839..2883
#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/1
msgid ""
"A lot of men died, and sometimes they stopped\n"
"work altogether.\n"
msgstr ""
"很多人死了，有时工程\n"
"干脆停工。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 2967..4193
#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/2
msgid ""
"This is one of those places. They had to cut\n"
"through steep terrain,\n"
msgstr ""
"这里就是其中之一。他们得穿过\n"
"陡峭地形，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 4207..5405
#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/3
msgid ""
"so when they finally made it through they just built\n"
"the rail terminal right there.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以好不容易打通后，就直接把\n"
"铁路终点站建在了那里。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 5447..5921
#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/4
msgid ""
"And that's why they named it...\n"
msgstr ""
"所以他们叫它……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0140_000_0
#. timeline 46138..64136
#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/5
msgid ""
"El Cadalso... the Gallows. Charming.\n"
msgstr ""
"El Cadalso……绞刑台。真迷人。\n"

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/6
msgid ""
"I'm surprised the construction money didn't dry up\n"
"the way things were going.\n"
msgstr ""
"照这情形，我很惊讶建设资金\n"
"没枯竭。\n"

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/7
msgid ""
"Actually, it did. But the bananas helped complete it,\n"
"so they say.\n"
msgstr ""
"其实确实枯竭了。但据说香蕉\n"
"帮忙建完了它。\n"

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/8
msgid ""
"You mean... the energy the workers got from\n"
"eating bananas?\n"
msgstr ""
"你是说……工人们吃香蕉\n"
"获得的能量？\n"

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/9
msgid ""
"I suppose they do have plenty of vitamins and...\n"
msgstr ""
"我想香蕉确实富含维生素和……\n"

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/10
msgid ""
"No, no, no, I meant the money they got to finish it\n"
"came from exporting bananas.\n"
msgstr ""
"不，不，不，我是说完工的钱\n"
"来自香蕉出口。\n"

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/11
#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/5
msgid ""
"Oh...\n"
msgstr ""
"哦……\n"

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/12
msgid ""
"But one thing is for certain!\n"
msgstr ""
"但有一点可以肯定！\n"

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/13
msgid ""
"The owners of the railroads expanded into the\n"
"banana trade\n"
msgstr ""
"铁路老板们扩张进了\n"
"香蕉贸易\n"

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/14
msgid ""
"after construction was completed.\n"
msgstr ""
"建设完工之后。\n"

#: codec/1/188/0xbcb50/15
msgid ""
"That was the start of banana cultivation in Costa\n"
"Rica.\n"
msgstr ""
"那就是哥斯达黎加香蕉种植的\n"
"开端。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 459..1741
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/0
msgid ""
"Snake, to the north of the village is a bridge that\n"
"crosses a hydraulic pipe,\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE，村子北边有座桥横跨\n"
"一条输水管，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 1783..2549
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/1
msgid ""
"though normally the bridge is not used by people.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过平时没人走那座桥。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 2577..3942
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/2
msgid ""
"If you slip you'll fall straight to the bottom of the\n"
"valley. Be careful.\n"
msgstr ""
"一滑就会直接摔到谷底。\n"
"小心点。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 4012..4500
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/3
msgid ""
"What's a channel doing here?\n"
msgstr ""
"这里怎么会有水渠？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 4527..5642
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/4
msgid ""
"It is not for irrigation - they're hydroelectric pipes.\n"
msgstr ""
"不是灌溉用的——是水力发电管。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 5767..6534
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/5
msgid ""
"I wonder if they run into Irazú's crater lake.\n"
msgstr ""
"不知是否通到伊拉苏火山口湖。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 6617..7509
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/6
msgid ""
"Normally they would build a reservoir at the\n"
"bottom of the valley,\n"
msgstr ""
"通常他们会在山谷底部\n"
"修建一座水库，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 7551..8247
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/7
msgid ""
"but it was probably too dangerous.\n"
msgstr ""
"但大概太危险了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0150_000_0
#. timeline 8373..9292
#: codec/1/189/0xbd110/8
msgid ""
"Los Cantos means \"Sword Peak.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"洛斯坎托斯意思是“剑峰”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 445..1476
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/0
msgid ""
"You should be able to see across the Irazú\n"
"mountain range from there.\n"
msgstr ""
"从那里应该能望见整个伊拉苏\n"
"山脉。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 1532..3078
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/1
msgid ""
"There are not as many big trees at that elevation,\n"
"and you'll probably be well above the mist.\n"
msgstr ""
"那个海拔大树不多，\n"
"而且你多半在雾层之上。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 3622..4193
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/2
msgid ""
"It'll be tough to hide up there.\n"
msgstr ""
"在那上面很难藏身。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 4221..5099
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/3
msgid ""
"You're not thinking about the scenery right now,\n"
"are you?\n"
msgstr ""
"你现在想的不是风景，\n"
"对吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 5154..5893
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/4
msgid ""
"Not while I'm surrounded by bad guys.\n"
msgstr ""
"被敌人围着的时候不会。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 5907..6617
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/5
msgid ""
"You should have seen it when the country was at\n"
"peace.\n"
msgstr ""
"你真该看看这个国家和平时的\n"
"样子。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 6729..7258
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/6
msgid ""
"I know you'd have been impressed.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道你一定会喜欢。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 7314..8874
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/7
msgid ""
"Well, that'll be our reward for a successful mission.\n"
"Sound good?\n"
msgstr ""
"那就当任务成功的奖励吧。\n"
"行吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0160_000_0
#. timeline 8902..9668
#: codec/1/189/0xbd460/8
msgid ""
"Wonderful. Thank you, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"太好了，谢谢SNAKE。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 445..1309
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/0
msgid ""
"...There is... an old fort around there.\n"
msgstr ""
"……那附近……有座旧堡垒。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 1309..2201
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/1
msgid ""
"What is it, Paz? You sound... upset.\n"
msgstr ""
"怎么了，帕兹？你听起来……不太对劲。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 2201..3705
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/2
msgid ""
"Well... You see, it was built during the civil war.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯……那是内战时期建的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 3733..5015
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/3
msgid ""
"Let me guess: disputes between Costa Rica's\n"
"political parties\n"
msgstr ""
"让我猜猜：哥斯达黎加各政党间的\n"
"争端\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 5015..5656
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/4
msgid ""
"escalated into all-out conflict.\n"
msgstr ""
"升级成了全面冲突。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 5656..6812
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/5
msgid ""
"Sí. Conflict that cost my grandparents their lives.\n"
msgstr ""
"是的。那场冲突夺走了我祖父母的命。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 6924..8303
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/6
msgid ""
"The most senseless sort of war - countrymen\n"
"mindlessly slaughtering their own.\n"
msgstr ""
"最无意义的战争——同胞\n"
"盲目地自相残杀。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 8345..9181
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/7
msgid ""
"That fort is a reminder of that senselessness.\n"
msgstr ""
"那座堡垒就是那场无谓战争的见证。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 9445..10518
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/8
msgid ""
"Sadly ironic, given who's occupying it now.\n"
msgstr ""
"讽刺的是，如今占领它的正是那些人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 10560..11479
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/9
msgid ""
"That war was the reason Costa Rica abolished the\n"
"army.\n"
msgstr ""
"那场战争让哥斯达黎加废除了\n"
"军队。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 11549..12371
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/10
msgid ""
"Please, Snake! Get them out of our country!\n"
msgstr ""
"求你了，SNAKE！把他们赶出我们的国家！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0170_000_0
#. timeline 12385..12928
#: codec/1/189/0xbd7c0/11
msgid ""
"I intend to.\n"
msgstr ""
"我正有此意。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 445..2410
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/0
msgid ""
"This area is a tropical cloud forest, continually\n"
"covered in a thick mist.\n"
msgstr ""
"这一地区是热带云雾林，常年\n"
"笼罩在浓密的雾气中。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 2465..3162
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/1
msgid ""
"It is quite a mystical place.\n"
msgstr ""
"是个很神秘的地方。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 3204..4987
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/2
msgid ""
"Selba de la Leche... \"Forest of Milk.\" I can barely\n"
"see in front of me.\n"
msgstr ""
"牛奶森林……“牛奶之林”。我几乎\n"
"看不清眼前。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 5015..6269
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/3
msgid ""
"There you go again. The forest is basically sitting\n"
"in a cloud,\n"
msgstr ""
"你又来了。这片森林基本上就是坐落在\n"
"云里，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 6283..7021
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/4
msgid ""
"so of course it's going to be hard to see.\n"
msgstr ""
"看不清是当然的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 7049..8623
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/5
msgid ""
"But you know, the cloud forest is the only place\n"
"many exotic creatures can live.\n"
msgstr ""
"但你知道，云雾林是许多奇异生物\n"
"唯一能生存的地方。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 8637..9849
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/6
msgid ""
"Well, if they're not edible, I'm not interested.\n"
msgstr ""
"不能吃的话我没兴趣。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 9905..10964
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/7
msgid ""
"Snake! I'll have you know people travel from all\n"
"around the world\n"
msgstr ""
"蛇！我告诉你，人们从世界\n"
"各地赶来\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0190_000_0
#. timeline 10964..11772
#: codec/1/190/0xbe2c0/8
msgid ""
"to witness Costa Rica's unique fauna!\n"
msgstr ""
"只为一睹哥斯达黎加独特的动物！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 445..1170
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/0
msgid ""
"Snake, watch out for the frogs.\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE，小心那些青蛙。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 1239..2883
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/1
msgid ""
"Why, they bite? Relax, no frog's ever eaten a snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"怎么，会咬人？放心，青蛙吃不了蛇。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 3009..4179
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/2
msgid ""
"Although I've feasted on a few frogs' legs myself...\n"
msgstr ""
"不过我自己倒是吃过几只蛙腿……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 4193..5029
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/3
msgid ""
"But, they're dangerous! They're poisonous!\n"
msgstr ""
"但它们很危险！有毒！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 5071..5335
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/4
msgid ""
"Poisonous?\n"
msgstr ""
"有毒？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 5335..6311
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/5
msgid ""
"Poison dart frogs live up to their name, I assure\n"
"you.\n"
msgstr ""
"箭毒蛙名副其实，我向你\n"
"保证。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 6380..7829
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/6
msgid ""
"Their poison is so strong the indígena use them to\n"
"make poison-tipped arrows.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们的毒性如此之强，原住民会用它们\n"
"制作毒箭。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 7857..9292
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/7
msgid ""
"Some secrete poison through their skin - even\n"
"touching them can be dangerous.\n"
msgstr ""
"有些通过皮肤分泌毒液——甚至\n"
"触碰它们都很危险。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 9292..9961
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/8
msgid ""
"So don't go petting them or anything.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以别去摸它们。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 10212..10978
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/9
msgid ""
"So... I can't eat one?\n"
msgstr ""
"我不能吃一个？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0200_000_0
#. timeline 10978..11424
#: codec/1/190/0xbe640/10
msgid ""
"I'm warning you!\n"
msgstr ""
"我警告你！\n"

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/0
msgid ""
"Catarata de la Muerte means \"Waterfall of Death.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"Catarata de la Muerte意为“死亡瀑布”。\n"

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/1
msgid ""
"How cheerful.\n"
msgstr ""
"真高兴。\n"

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/2
msgid ""
"I am sure it will be no problem for you, Snake,\n"
msgstr ""
"我相信这对你不在话下，SNAKE，\n"

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/3
msgid ""
"especially compared to all the dire situations\n"
"you've faced in the past.\n"
msgstr ""
"尤其是与你过去所面对的\n"
"那些可怕处境相比。\n"

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/4
msgid ""
"Easy to say now. We'll see what really happens.\n"
msgstr ""
"现在说得轻巧。到时候看吧。\n"

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/5
msgid ""
"Sorry. Still, you have surprised me. Everything they\n"
"say about the legend is true.\n"
msgstr ""
"抱歉。不过你让我吃惊了。关于传说的\n"
"一切果然都是真的。\n"

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/6
msgid ""
"I'm neither hero nor legend. But for some reason, I\n"
"don't mind you calling me that.\n"
msgstr ""
"我既非英雄也非传说。但不知为何，\n"
"我不介意你这么叫。\n"

#: codec/1/190/0xbe9e0/7
msgid ""
"Thanks. Be careful, Snake. Peace!\n"
msgstr ""
"谢谢。小心点，SNAKE。和平！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 445..1309
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/0
msgid ""
"La Ruinas de Xochiquetzal will be around there.\n"
msgstr ""
"索奇克察尔遗迹就在那附近。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 1337..2619
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/1
msgid ""
"They have not been restored at all, so they may\n"
"well be covered in plants.\n"
msgstr ""
"它们完全没被修复过，所以很可能\n"
"被植物覆盖了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 2702..3106
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/2
msgid ""
"Xochiquetzal?\n"
msgstr ""
"索奇克察尔？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 3134..3970
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/3
msgid ""
"An Aztec goddess of fertility and beauty.\n"
msgstr ""
"阿兹特克的丰饶与美丽女神。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 4068..5154
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/4
msgid ""
"They say she was always accompanied by birds\n"
"and butterflies.\n"
msgstr ""
"据说她身边总有鸟儿\n"
"和蝴蝶相伴。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 5210..6506
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/5
msgid ""
"One theory states she was the mother of the god\n"
"known as Quetzalcoatl.\n"
msgstr ""
"有一种说法称她是神明\n"
"魁札尔科亚特尔之母。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 6575..6993
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/6
msgid ""
"Quetzalcoatl...\n"
msgstr ""
"羽蛇神……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 7035..8400
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/7
msgid ""
"The quetzal is said to be an incarnation of\n"
"Quetzalcoatl, hence its name.\n"
msgstr ""
"凤尾绿咬鹃据说是羽蛇神的化身，\n"
"因此得名。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 8442..10309
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/8
msgid ""
"I get it. Well, this place definitely matches the\n"
"atmosphere of a cloud forest.\n"
msgstr ""
"明白了。这地方确实符合\n"
"云雾林的气氛。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 10323..11535
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/9
msgid ""
"Now, it may have seen better days, but that is still\n"
"a temple.\n"
msgstr ""
"虽说它已不复往昔，但那仍是\n"
"一座神庙。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 11591..12399
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/10
msgid ""
"So, be sure to show respect when you're inside.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以进去后务必表示敬意。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 12427..12901
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/11
msgid ""
"If the mood strikes me.\n"
msgstr ""
"看我心情。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 12956..14001
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/12
msgid ""
"Hmph! Well, you've got no one to blame but yourself\n"
msgstr ""
"哼！那要是索奇克察尔惩罚你，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0230_000_0
#. timeline 14043..14698
#: codec/1/191/0xbf3b0/13
msgid ""
"if Xochiquetzal strikes you down.\n"
msgstr ""
"你也只能怪自己。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 445..1434
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/0
msgid ""
"I do not know if I recall such large ruins being\n"
"there...\n"
msgstr ""
"我不记得那里有\n"
"如此庞大的遗迹……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 1630..2897
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/1
msgid ""
"Well, didn't you say there's a lot we don't know\n"
"about Costa Rica's ancient civilizations?\n"
msgstr ""
"你不是说哥斯达黎加的古文明\n"
"还有很多未知吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 2925..4193
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/2
msgid ""
"You talked about some giant stone balls, too. What\n"
"are those?\n"
msgstr ""
"你也提到过一些巨大的石球。那些\n"
"是什么？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 4235..5154
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/3
msgid ""
"Oh, the Stone Spheres of Costa Rica?\n"
msgstr ""
"哦，哥斯达黎加石球？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 5266..6074
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/4
msgid ""
"They're an assortment of giant spheres carved\n"
"from stone\n"
msgstr ""
"它们是一批石雕的巨大球体，\n"
"种类繁多\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 6074..7383
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/5
msgid ""
"that were discovered in the jungles of Costa Rica\n"
"about 50 years ago.\n"
msgstr ""
"大约50年前在哥斯达黎加的丛林中被\n"
"发现。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 7411..7941
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/6
msgid ""
"What's so special about that?\n"
msgstr ""
"那有什么特别的？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 7983..9041
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/7
msgid ""
"What if I told you some of them are nearly perfect\n"
"spheres?\n"
msgstr ""
"如果我告诉你其中一些几乎是完美\n"
"球体呢？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 9167..10407
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/8
msgid ""
"And that they were carved out of granite, which is\n"
"quite a hard substance.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且它们由花岗岩雕成，这是一种\n"
"相当坚硬的物质。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 10448..11493
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/9
msgid ""
"Hmm, could be good for laying a trap.\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯，用来设陷阱不错。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 11605..12483
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/10
msgid ""
"And if they're spherical, they'd roll easily, too...\n"
msgstr ""
"球形的还容易滚动……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0240_000_0
#. timeline 12496..12845
#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice 
#. timeline 1017..1281
#: codec/1/191/0xbf890/11
#: codec/2/902/0x3861c0/8
#: codec/2/903/0x3879e0/1
#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/0
#: codec/2/910/0x38e660/0
#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/0
#: codec/2/911/0x38f200/14
msgid ""
"Snake...\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0250_000_0
#. timeline 445..1365
#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/0
msgid ""
"So tell me, what do they mine around here?\n"
msgstr ""
"那这附近采什么矿？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0250_000_0
#. timeline 1393..1936
#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/1
msgid ""
"Gold, if I am not mistaken.\n"
msgstr ""
"没记错，是金矿。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0250_000_0
#. timeline 1978..3733
#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/2
msgid ""
"Gold?! No kidding. I wonder what'd be the fastest\n"
"way to...\n"
msgstr ""
"黄金？！没开玩笑吧。我想知道最快的\n"
"办法是什么……\n"

#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/3
msgid ""
"I do not know how much success they've had.\n"
msgstr ""
"不知道他们收益如何。\n"

#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/4
msgid ""
"You do not hear of anyone still operating mines\n"
"around here.\n"
msgstr ""
"你没听说这附近还有人仍在经营\n"
"矿场。\n"

#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/6
msgid ""
"Generally speaking, people here are not too thrilled\n"
"with outside capital\n"
msgstr ""
"一般来说，这里的人对外来资本\n"
"并不太欢迎\n"

#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/7
msgid ""
"coming in and taking away the country's natural\n"
"resources.\n"
msgstr ""
"进来并拿走这个国家的自然\n"
"资源。\n"

#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/8
msgid ""
"Four years ago, a group of protestors hurled\n"
"stones at the parliament building\n"
msgstr ""
"四年前，一群抗议者向\n"
"议会大楼投掷石块\n"

#: codec/1/191/0xbfcf0/9
msgid ""
"when people found out the country had been\n"
"bestowing mining rights to foreign companies.\n"
msgstr ""
"当人们发现这个国家一直在\n"
"将采矿权授予外国公司时。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 445..1783
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/0
msgid ""
"They must have had to clear a considerable\n"
"amount of forest to open up that mine.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们肯定不得不清理相当\n"
"数量的森林来开辟那座矿场。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 2020..3092
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/1
msgid ""
"No doubt. So much for any hiding places, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。藏身之处也没了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 3120..4207
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/2
msgid ""
"And it is not just the forest. Without the proper\n"
"precautions,\n"
msgstr ""
"而且不仅是森林。如果没有适当\n"
"预防措施，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 4277..5113
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/3
msgid ""
"the mine's waste water could pollute the\n"
"groundwater.\n"
msgstr ""
"矿场的废水可能会污染\n"
"地下水。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 5182..6339
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/4
msgid ""
"And to top it all off, they're developing nuclear\n"
"weapons there, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"最糟糕的是，他们还在那里开发核\n"
"武器。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 6450..7328
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/5
msgid ""
"How can people care so little about their own\n"
"country?\n"
msgstr ""
"人们怎么能对自己国家\n"
"如此漠不关心？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 7370..8038
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/6
msgid ""
"...I'm not the one to ask about that.\n"
msgstr ""
"……这问题别问我。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 8038..8930
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/7
msgid ""
"Well, you may have abandoned your country,\n"
msgstr ""
"你也许抛弃了自己的国家，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 9055..9752
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/8
msgid ""
"but you still treasure where you came from.\n"
msgstr ""
"但你依然珍视自己的故乡。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 10198..10504
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/9
#: codec/1/235/0xeb860/10
#: codec/2/914/0x392460/23
msgid ""
"You think so?\n"
msgstr ""
"是吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e55d959 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 10518..11312
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/10
msgid ""
"Sure. I know you do.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然。我知道你是这样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_paz0260_000_0
#. timeline 11424..13931
#: codec/1/192/0xc00b0/11
msgid ""
"Paz, you... I... Whatever you do, never stop loving\n"
"your country.\n"
msgstr ""
"帕兹，你……我……无论你做什么，永远不要停止热爱\n"
"your country。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/0
msgid ""
"Since it was founded, my country has not once\n"
"been able to choose its own path.\n"
msgstr ""
"自建国以来，我的国家从未\n"
"能够选择自己的道路。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/1
msgid ""
"First Spain, then America. Over one hundred years\n"
"of this...\n"
msgstr ""
"先是西班牙，然后是美洲。一百多年来\n"
"都是如此……\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/2
#: codec/1/197/0xc5540/11
msgid ""
"I know.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/3
msgid ""
"In the 19th century,\n"
msgstr ""
"19世纪，\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/4
msgid ""
"an American mercenary named William Walker\n"
"seized power in Nicaragua.\n"
msgstr ""
"一位名叫威廉·沃克的美国雇佣兵\n"
"夺取了尼加拉瓜的政权。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/5
msgid ""
"I'd heard he exploited rivalries between the political\n"
"parties.\n"
msgstr ""
"我听说他利用了政党之间的\n"
"敌对关系。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/6
msgid ""
"Even after we expelled him,\n"
msgstr ""
"即便我们赶走他，\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/7
msgid ""
"the Americans sent in their Marines under the\n"
"pretext of quelling political unrest.\n"
msgstr ""
"美国人以平息政治动乱为\n"
"借口，派出了他们的海军陆战队。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/8
msgid ""
"And the real reason?\n"
msgstr ""
"真正原因？\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc04e0/9
msgid ""
"To intimidate the government and thwart the\n"
"construction of the Nicaragua Canal.\n"
msgstr ""
"为了恐吓政府并阻挠\n"
"尼加拉瓜运河的建设。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0880/0
msgid ""
"I thought the U.S. already has the rights to build a\n"
"canal in Nicaragua...\n"
msgstr ""
"我以为美国已经拥有在尼加拉瓜\n"
"修建运河的权利……\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0880/1
msgid ""
"They never intended to build a canal there. They\n"
"had already started digging in Panama.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们从未打算在那里修建运河。他们\n"
"已经在巴拿马开始挖掘了。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0880/2
msgid ""
"A canal in Nicaragua would break up the Panama\n"
"Canal's monopoly,\n"
msgstr ""
"尼加拉瓜的运河会打破巴拿马\n"
"运河的垄断，\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0880/3
msgid ""
"reason enough for America to stick its nose into\n"
"our affairs.\n"
msgstr ""
"这足以让美国插手\n"
"我们的事务。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0880/4
msgid ""
"They snagged the rights so nobody else could\n"
"build there...\n"
msgstr ""
"他们抢了权利，别人就没法\n"
"在那修建……\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0880/5
msgid ""
"It was General Sandino who finally stood up to los\n"
"yanquis.\n"
msgstr ""
"是桑地诺将军最终挺身对抗\n"
"美国佬。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/0
msgid ""
"General Sandino waged a guerrilla war against the\n"
"Marines,\n"
msgstr ""
"桑地诺将军对海军陆战队\n"
"发动了游击战，\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/1
msgid ""
"at last driving them out. He was a true hero, and -\n"
"to us Sandinistas - like a father.\n"
msgstr ""
"最终赶走了他们。他是真英雄，\n"
"对我们桑地诺人，就像父亲。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/2
msgid ""
"But when they pulled out, the Americans left us\n"
"something to remember them by.\n"
msgstr ""
"但他们撤走时，美国人留给我们\n"
"一样东西作纪念。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/3
msgid ""
"The National Guard.\n"
msgstr ""
"国民警卫队。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/4
msgid ""
"Yes, la Guardia. In name, a peacekeeping force.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错，国民警卫队。名义上是维和部队。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/5
msgid ""
"But in reality, Commander Somoza's personal army,\n"
"answering to no one else.\n"
msgstr ""
"实际上是索摩查司令的私人军队，\n"
"只听命于他一人。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/6
msgid ""
"Unable to stay silent, General Sandino went to\n"
"protest...\n"
msgstr ""
"桑地诺将军无法保持沉默，前去\n"
"抗议……\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/7
msgid ""
"and was assassinated by Somoza as he made his\n"
"way home.\n"
msgstr ""
"并在回家的路上\n"
"被索摩查暗杀。\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/8
msgid ""
"It was then that Somoza and los sapos\n"
msgstr ""
"就在那时，索摩查和蟾蜍\n"

#: codec/1/192/0xc0b40/9
msgid ""
"began to eat our country alive, from the inside.\n"
msgstr ""
"开始从内部活活吞噬我们的国家。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/0
msgid ""
"The first Somoza was originally no more than the\n"
"commander of la Guardia.\n"
msgstr ""
"第一代索摩查原本不过是\n"
"国民警卫队的司令。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/1
msgid ""
"Ordinarily, a man of his station could never hope to\n"
"become president.\n"
msgstr ""
"按常理，以他的身份绝无可能\n"
"当上总统。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/2
msgid ""
"But the president at the time had no power to\n"
"back him.\n"
msgstr ""
"但当时的总统无力\n"
"支持他。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/3
msgid ""
"The only one with the strength to oppose him was\n"
"General Sandino.\n"
msgstr ""
"唯一有力量反对他的，只有\n"
"桑地诺将军。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/4
msgid ""
"....No. Better to say the General was the only one\n"
"who dared oppose him.\n"
msgstr ""
"……不。不如说，将军是唯一\n"
"敢于反对他的人。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/5
msgid ""
"There was nothing special about him.\n"
msgstr ""
"他并没有什么特别之处。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/6
msgid ""
"Above all, it takes a strong will to see justice done.\n"
"That is what he taught us.\n"
msgstr ""
"关键是，伸张正义需坚强意志。\n"
"这是他教我们的。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/7
msgid ""
"It's also what motivated Somoza to have him killed...\n"
msgstr ""
"也正是这一点促使索摩查杀了他……\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/8
msgid ""
"Yes. The rest was easy. He got rid of the\n"
"president, taking office in a sham election.\n"
msgstr ""
"是的。剩下的就简单了。他除掉了\n"
"总统，靠一场假选举上台。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/9
msgid ""
"And once he had power, he never gave it up.\n"
msgstr ""
"一旦掌权，他就再也没放手。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/10
msgid ""
"Talk about heavy-handed.\n"
msgstr ""
"真是够强硬的。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/11
msgid ""
"He had the Americans backing him, that's why.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是因为有美国人给他撑腰。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/12
msgid ""
"They didn't want to hand over power to a\n"
"rebellious general.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们不想把权力交给一个\n"
"叛逆的将军。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/13
msgid ""
"Even so, it's hard to believe Washington would give\n"
"its blessing to a guy like that.\n"
msgstr ""
"即便如此，也很难相信华盛顿会\n"
"祝福那种家伙。\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/14
msgid ""
"The American President at the time put it this way:\n"
msgstr ""
"当时的美国总统是这么说的：\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/15
msgid ""
"\"Somoza may be a son of a bitch, but he's our son\n"
"of a bitch.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“索摩查也许是个狗娘养的，但他是\n"
"咱们的狗娘养的。”\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/16
msgid ""
"In other words, better a dog or los sapos (Somoza\n"
"and counter-revolutionaries)\n"
msgstr ""
"换句话说，宁可要条狗或蟾蜍（索摩查\n"
"和反革命分子）\n"

#: codec/1/193/0xc16a0/17
msgid ""
"than an anti-US regime.\n"
msgstr ""
"比反美政权更甚。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/0
msgid ""
"The river that flows between Nicaragua and Costa\n"
"Rica is el Río San Juan.\n"
msgstr ""
"流经尼加拉瓜和哥斯\n"
"黎巴嫩之间的河流是圣胡安河。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/1
msgid ""
"It connects Lago Cocibolca to el Mar Caribe.\n"
msgstr ""
"它连接科西博尔卡湖与加勒比海。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/2
msgid ""
"It is a gentle river, safe even for small boats. You\n"
"have to watch out for the sharks, though.\n"
msgstr ""
"这是一条平缓的河流，连小船也能安全通行。不过\n"
"你得小心鲨鱼。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/3
msgid ""
"Sharks? In a river?\n"
msgstr ""
"鲨鱼？在河？\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/4
msgid ""
"El tiburón toro live in the river. But there's nothing\n"
"to fear. San Juan will protect you always.\n"
msgstr ""
"公牛鲨生活在河里。但没什么\n"
"好怕的。圣胡安会永远保护你。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/5
msgid ""
"Juan?\n"
msgstr ""
"胡安？\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/6
msgid ""
"The Rio San Juan takes its name from San Juan,\n"
"the man who baptized Jesús.\n"
msgstr ""
"圣胡安河得名于圣胡安，\n"
"就是为耶稣施洗的人。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/7
msgid ""
"The man you call John the Baptist in your country.\n"
msgstr ""
"在你们国家叫施洗约翰。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2170/8
msgid ""
"John, huh... I'll be careful anyway. I'd hate to drown\n"
"- end up a John Doe.\n"
msgstr ""
"约翰，嗯……我还是小心点。我可不想淹死\n"
"成无名氏。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/0
msgid ""
"There is a volcanic island in Lago Cocibolca called\n"
"Ometepe.\n"
msgstr ""
"科西博尔卡湖有座火山岛，名叫\n"
"奥梅特佩。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/1
msgid ""
"It's formed from two connected volcanoes, shaped\n"
"like a porongo (gourd).\n"
msgstr ""
"它由两座相连火山构成，形状\n"
"像葫芦（porongo）。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/2
msgid ""
"The one with smoke coming out of it?\n"
msgstr ""
"就是那座冒烟的？\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/3
msgid ""
"That's the one. The smoking volcano is\n"
"Concepción. It erupts once in a while.\n"
msgstr ""
"就是那座。冒烟的火山是\n"
"康塞普西翁。它偶尔喷发。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/4
msgid ""
"The other one is Maderas.\n"
msgstr ""
"另一座是马德拉斯。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/5
msgid ""
"It's never erupted in recorded history. There's a\n"
"lake in the caldera at the top.\n"
msgstr ""
"有历史记录以来它从未喷发过。山顶的\n"
"火山口里有一个湖。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/6
msgid ""
"A crater lake... Let's hope there's not another\n"
"underground factory inside...\n"
msgstr ""
"火山口湖……希望里面没有另一个\n"
"地下工厂……\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/7
msgid ""
"Don't say that!\n"
msgstr ""
"别这么说！\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/8
msgid ""
"If Peace Walker's nukes detonated there, it would\n"
"destabilize the magma underneath.\n"
msgstr ""
"如果和平行者号的核弹在那里引爆，会\n"
"破坏下方岩浆的稳定。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/9
msgid ""
"It could cause the volcano to erupt again.\n"
msgstr ""
"可能导致火山再次喷发。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2510/10
msgid ""
"If that happens, my country is doomed. Snake, you\n"
"must stop Peace Walker!\n"
msgstr ""
"那样我国就完了。斯内克，你\n"
"必须阻止和平行者！\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/0
msgid ""
"We are Sandinistas, the heirs of General Sandino's\n"
"will.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们是桑地诺人，继承桑地诺将军\n"
"遗志。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/1
msgid ""
"Sandino... the father of modern guerrilla warfare.\n"
msgstr ""
"桑地诺……现代游击战之父。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/2
msgid ""
"To you, maybe. To us, he's more like a real father.\n"
msgstr ""
"对你或许。对我们，他更像真父亲。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/3
msgid ""
"That why you named yourselves after him?\n"
msgstr ""
"所以你们以他命名？\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/4
msgid ""
"Of course. La Frente Sandinista de Liberación\n"
"Nacional...\n"
msgstr ""
"当然。桑地诺民族解放\n"
"阵线……\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/5
msgid ""
"the Sandinista National Liberation Front is named\n"
"in his honor.\n"
msgstr ""
"桑地诺民族解放阵线以\n"
"他命名，以示纪念。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/6
msgid ""
"We share the General's goal - to take back our\n"
"country's freedom.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们和将军目标一致，夺回我们\n"
"国家的自由。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/7
msgid ""
"In his day, from America. In ours, from the despot\n"
"Somoza.\n"
msgstr ""
"他那时，敌人来自美国。我们这时，敌人是暴君\n"
"索摩查。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/8
msgid ""
"Times have changed, but the song remains the\n"
"same.\n"
msgstr ""
"时代变了，但歌还是那首\n"
"歌。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/9
msgid ""
"\"Patria Libre o Morir\"... That is our slogan.\n"
msgstr ""
"“自由祖国或死亡”……这是我们的口号。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/10
msgid ""
"El Che used to say the same thing, you know?\n"
msgstr ""
"切也曾说过同样的话。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/11
msgid ""
"\"Patria o Muerte\"... the slogan of the Cuban\n"
"Revolution.\n"
msgstr ""
"“祖国或死亡”……古巴\n"
"革命的标语。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/12
msgid ""
"So you're fighting for a socialist revolution, too,\n"
"then?\n"
msgstr ""
"这么说你们也是在为社会主义革命而战，\n"
"是吗？\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/13
msgid ""
"No. It's not about ideology. We only want to live\n"
"normal lives.\n"
msgstr ""
"不。无关意识形态。我们只想\n"
"正常生活。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/14
msgid ""
"We are sick of living in a country where you can\n"
"be beaten for walking down the street.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们受够了生活在一个可能因为走在街上\n"
"就被殴打的国家。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/15
msgid ""
"Where you never know if your neighbor is snitching\n"
"on you.\n"
msgstr ""
"在那儿，你不知邻居会不会背后\n"
"告发你。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/16
msgid ""
"Our goal is to give back the country to its people.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们的目标是把国家还给人民。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/17
msgid ""
"Yeah. The Cuban Revolution started out like that,\n"
"too...\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊。古巴革命当初也这样开始，\n"
"也是……\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/18
msgid ""
"We are few in number, but we will win.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们人少，但会赢。\n"

#: codec/1/194/0xc2950/19
msgid ""
"Victoria o muerte. For a revolutionary, there is no\n"
"other fate.\n"
msgstr ""
"胜利或死亡。对革命者来说，没有\n"
"别的命运。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/0
msgid ""
"Augusto César Sandino... general and hero of\n"
"Nicaragua.\n"
msgstr ""
"奥古斯托·塞萨尔·桑地诺……尼加拉瓜的\n"
"将军和英雄。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/1
msgid ""
"Fifty years ago, conflict broke out between the\n"
"political parties of Nicaragua.\n"
msgstr ""
"五十年前，尼加拉瓜各政党之间\n"
"爆发了冲突。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/2
msgid ""
"The U.S. Marines intervened in the name of\n"
"restoring order.\n"
msgstr ""
"美国海军陆战队以恢复秩序为名\n"
"干预。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/3
msgid ""
"The only one who refused to listen to their call for\n"
"reconciliation was General Sandino.\n"
msgstr ""
"唯一拒绝响应他们和解呼吁的人，\n"
"就是桑地诺将军。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/4
msgid ""
"One man against the Marines... That takes guts.\n"
msgstr ""
"一人对抗海军陆战队……真有种。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/5
msgid ""
"The General wasn't a professional soldier. Neither\n"
"were his compadres.\n"
msgstr ""
"将军不是职业军人。他的\n"
"兄弟们也不是。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/6
msgid ""
"And they certainly could not match the Marines'\n"
"equipment.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们当然无法匹敌海军陆战队的\n"
"装备。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/7
msgid ""
"But he used the land to his advantage, lurking in\n"
"the fields and hills of Nicaragua,\n"
msgstr ""
"但他利用地形优势，潜伏在\n"
"尼加拉瓜的田野和山丘之中，\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/8
msgid ""
"and using surprise attacks to harass the Marines.\n"
msgstr ""
"用突袭骚扰海军陆战队。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/9
msgid ""
"I know. I've read plenty of textbooks on guerrilla\n"
"warfare.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道。我读过不少关于游击战的\n"
"教科书。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/10
msgid ""
"In the end, he drove them out. He was truly a role\n"
"model for us.\n"
msgstr ""
"最终，他赶走了他们。他真是我们的\n"
"榜样。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/11
msgid ""
"Yeah, but that was the '30s - didn't the Depression\n"
"have something to do with it?\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，但那是30年代——大萧条\n"
"跟这没关系吗？\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/12
msgid ""
"It takes cash to wage war.\n"
msgstr ""
"打仗得花钱。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/13
msgid ""
"Perhaps. But there is no denying what the General\n"
"accomplished.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许吧。但将军的成就\n"
"无可否认。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/14
msgid ""
"The people hailed him as the \"General de Hombres\n"
"Libres\" - the general of free men.\n"
msgstr ""
"人民称他为“自由人将军”\n"
"——General de Hombres Libres。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/15
msgid ""
"They loved him. And then...\n"
msgstr ""
"他们爱戴他。然后……\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/16
msgid ""
"He was assassinated - by Anastasio Somoza\n"
"Garcia, commander of la Guardia.\n"
msgstr ""
"他被暗杀了——凶手是安纳斯塔西奥·索摩查·\n"
"加西亚，国民警卫队司令。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/17
msgid ""
"The father of the current Somoza.\n"
msgstr ""
"现任索摩查的父亲。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/18
msgid ""
"Somoza had the Americans' backing. That is the\n"
"way things were.\n"
msgstr ""
"索摩查有美国人的支持。事情\n"
"就是这样。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/19
msgid ""
"The General may be dead, and the times may have\n"
"changed,\n"
msgstr ""
"将军可能已经死了，时代可能已经\n"
"变了，\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/20
msgid ""
"but his will lives on inside each of us.\n"
msgstr ""
"但他意志活在我们每人心中。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc3080/21
msgid ""
"We are the sons and daughters of General Sandino.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们是桑地诺将军的儿女。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/0
msgid ""
"Hey. How's the watermelon business these days?\n"
msgstr ""
"嘿，最近西瓜生意怎么样？\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/1
msgid ""
"Not bad. I hear the compas back home are hanging\n"
"in there, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"不错。我听说家乡的同志们也\n"
"在坚持。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/2
msgid ""
"Good to hear.\n"
msgstr ""
"那就好。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/3
msgid ""
"...You know our nickname. I'm impressed.\n"
msgstr ""
"……你竟知我们绰号，佩服。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/4
msgid ""
"No wonder they call you Boss.\n"
msgstr ""
"难怪人家叫你BOSS。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/5
msgid ""
"You used to hide your weapons in hollowed-out\n"
"watermelons,\n"
msgstr ""
"你们以前把武器藏在挖空的\n"
"西瓜里，\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/6
msgid ""
"smuggle 'em right past the National Guard.\n"
msgstr ""
"就这么混过国民警卫队。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/7
msgid ""
"You even transported pineapple grenades that\n"
"way.\n"
msgstr ""
"你们甚至那样\n"
"运菠萝手榴弹。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/8
msgid ""
"The name caught on among sympathizers in the\n"
"region and...\n"
msgstr ""
"这名字在地区同情者中\n"
"传开，而且……\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/9
#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/39
#: codec/2/914/0x392460/18
msgid ""
"What are you talking about?\n"
msgstr ""
"你在说什么？\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/11
msgid ""
"They call us watermelon sellers because the\n"
"General's name\n"
msgstr ""
"他们叫我们西瓜贩子，因为\n"
"将军的名字\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/12
msgid ""
"sounds like the word for watermelon, sandía.\n"
msgstr ""
"听起来像西瓜，sandía。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/13
#: codec/1/215/0xd79a0/9
msgid ""
"...Really?\n"
msgstr ""
"…真？\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/14
msgid ""
"Si.\n"
msgstr ""
"是。\n"

#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/15
msgid ""
"Dammit, Kaz...\n"
msgstr ""
"可恶，卡兹…\n"

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/0
msgid ""
"I noticed you call Che Guevara \"El Che.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"你管切·格瓦拉叫“El Che”。\n"

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/1
msgid ""
"Not just us. Everyone in these parts does.\n"
msgstr ""
"不只我们。这的人都这么叫。\n"

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/2
msgid ""
"\"Che\" was always his nickname. It does not feel\n"
"right to call him by his last name.\n"
msgstr ""
"“切”一直是他的昵称。叫他\n"
"姓，感觉不对。\n"

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/3
msgid ""
"...I was shocked the first time I saw you. You look\n"
"so much like him.\n"
msgstr ""
"…我第一次见你时很震惊。你太像\n"
"他了。\n"

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/4
msgid ""
"I look like \"El Che\", huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"我像“El Che”？\n"

#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/5
msgid ""
"Sort of. Not in the face. It's more... the way you\n"
"carry yourself...\n"
msgstr ""
"有点像。不是脸。更像是…你的\n"
"举手投足…\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 7397..8136
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/6
msgid ""
"I guess Che's a hero to the Sandinistas, too?\n"
msgstr ""
"切对桑地诺派来说也是英雄吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 8164..10156
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/7
msgid ""
"Of course. The FSLN was formed in the spirit of\n"
"the ideologies championed by El Che and Fidel.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然。FSLN正是本着El Che和\n"
"菲德尔所倡导的思想成立的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 10421..12775
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/8
msgid ""
"Fidel... Fidel Castro. So you're trying to bring the\n"
"Cuban Revolution to Nicaragua.\n"
msgstr ""
"菲德尔…卡斯特罗。你们想把\n"
"古巴革命带到尼加拉瓜。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 12845..14642
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/9
msgid ""
"Well, we were. But Cuba isn't what it once was...\n"
"Not since El Che left.\n"
msgstr ""
"曾经是。但古巴已不复当年…\n"
"自El Che走后。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 14740..16314
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/10
msgid ""
"El Che was a true revolutionary. He fought - and\n"
"died - for the people.\n"
msgstr ""
"El Che是真正的革命者。他为人民\n"
"战斗——并牺牲。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 16370..17387
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/11
msgid ""
"He worked harder than anybody, and he was a\n"
"righteous man.\n"
msgstr ""
"他比谁都努力，他是个\n"
"正直的人。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 17442..19045
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/12
msgid ""
"Even as a minister of Cuba, he gave up his\n"
"weekends to work on the farms and public works.\n"
msgstr ""
"即使身为古巴部长，他也放弃周末\n"
"去农场和公共工程干活。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 19100..19560
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/13
msgid ""
"As a volunteer, no less.\n"
msgstr ""
"还是当志愿者。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 19644..20271
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/14
msgid ""
"Yeah, I've heard the stories.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，故事我听过。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 20326..21441
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/15
msgid ""
"But when you think about it, wasn't it that\n"
"obsession that did him in?\n"
msgstr ""
"但想想看，不正是那份\n"
"执念害了他吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 21483..21831
#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0010_000_0
#. timeline 2048..2326
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/16
#: codec/1/241/0xf15f0/1
msgid ""
"How do you mean?\n"
msgstr ""
"什么意思？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 21887..23517
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/17
msgid ""
"We can't all be supermen. He thought the ideals he\n"
"applied in Cuba would work in Bolivia.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们不可能都是超人。他以为古巴\n"
"行得通的理想，玻利维亚也行。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 23558..25077
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/18
msgid ""
"But, he failed to win converts and the support of\n"
"the peasants, and it cost him his life.\n"
msgstr ""
"但他没能争取到皈依者和\n"
"农民的支持，为此丢了命。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 25175..25927
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/19
msgid ""
"Maybe... maybe you're right.\n"
msgstr ""
"也许…你说得对。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e3bb338 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 26010..27278
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/20
msgid ""
"But at least he did not steal from those peasants,\n"
"no matter how hard things got.\n"
msgstr ""
"但至少他没偷农民的东西，\n"
"再难也没偷。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_amd0090_000_0
#. timeline 27320..27473
#. speaker 0x0ea8e31c voice v_bri_huy0210_000_0
#. timeline 1309..1476
#: codec/1/196/0xc4280/21
#: codec/1/201/0xc9700/14
#: codec/1/206/0xce040/7
#: codec/1/225/0xe1160/2
#: codec/1/254/0xfe0a0/1
#: codec/2/908/0x38c3b0/12
#: codec/2/913/0x391bb0/1
msgid ""
"Yeah.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊。\n"
